What:		/sys/class/power_supply/USB/device/vbus_test
What:		/sys/class/power_supply/bq256xx-charger/device/vbus_test
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	ichinomoto <ichinomoto@gmail.com>
Description:
		Manual, leased VBUS output for Pomera DM200, DM250 and DM250US.
		DM200/DM250 require the RK818 otg-vbus-supply DT property.
		DM250US requires BQ25620 and ti,manual-vbus-control in DT; the
		attributes belong to its physical I2C device, not the supply kobject.
		Other boards and BQ variants do not expose this interface.
		Read: 1 when this driver has enabled the OTG output, otherwise 0.
		This is software state, not a connector voltage measurement.
		Write: 1..30 enables output for that many seconds; 0 stops it.
		Repeating a nonzero write cannot extend a running lease (EBUSY).
		Root writes only. No output is started at boot, resume or replug.
		External VBUS present at start returns EBUSY, using raw input
		indications while output is OFF. BQ25620 also requires a fresh,
		bounded, VBUS-only ADC conversion at or below 400 mV, because a
		raw VBUS type of zero does not prove absence of input with automatic
		detection disabled. ADC/I2C errors refuse output. Saved ADC settings
		are restored. BQ25620 HIZ or forced D+/D- detection refuses startup.
		It uses direct EN_OTG control at 5.04 V / 1 A and verifies actual
		boost entry after the hardware's 30-ms delay. Before enabling,
		userspace must
		warn that chargers, PCs and VBUS-sourcing hubs MUST NOT be connected
		until output has been successfully stopped (vbus_ctl off).
		External supply insertion during output cannot be reliably
		distinguished from our own voltage. Logical suppression of our own
		output in charger reporting is not an independent external-power
		sensor. This interface provides no electrical collision protection.
		Charging is paused before enabling output and restored only
		after successfully disabling it (with BQ25620 OFF readback before
		restoring D+/D- policy and charging). Failed OFF remains non-renewable
		and keeps charging paused; the running kernel retries timed and
		explicit OFF failures. Suspend, hibernate, shutdown and driver unbind
		stop output. A failed OFF prevents suspend. Resume never starts it.
		Timeout requires a running kernel; it cannot recover a hardware hang.

What:		/sys/class/power_supply/USB/device/vbus_keepalive
What:		/sys/class/power_supply/bq256xx-charger/device/vbus_keepalive
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	ichinomoto <ichinomoto@gmail.com>
Description:
		Root-only, write-only renewal for an existing leased VBUS output.
		Write 1..30 to replace its deadline with that many seconds from now.
		Output must already be enabled, unexpired and not stopping,
		suspended or shutting down; otherwise ESHUTDOWN is returned.
		This never starts output. Invalid durations return EINVAL before
		checking output state, as for vbus_test.
		Healthy userspace monitoring may renew indefinitely: there is no
		total session limit, but each individual kernel lease is at most
		30 seconds. Userspace must verify USB device enumeration before
		renewing and stop output on disconnect or host-off. If userspace
		exits or hangs, the last deadline expires in at most 30 seconds
		while the kernel runs. Use vbus_test=0 for an immediate stop.
		All external-power restrictions and charging pause/restore behavior
		of vbus_test still apply.
